    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Benefits of tourism",
      "text": "Tourism can support development through spending, employment, foreign exchange, infrastructure, facilities and cultural exchange. A benefit should be explained through a mechanism and the people receiving it. Counting arrivals alone does not establish how much income stays locally or how widely it is shared. The size and distribution of benefits depend on ownership, employment arrangements, sourcing, visitor behaviour and management.",
