      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Visitor spending creates receipts for accommodation providers, guides, food sellers, transport operators and other enterprises. These receipts can pay wages, local suppliers and operating costs. A portion may become profit or finance reinvestment. Sales revenue is not the same as profit or local household income. A lodge collecting N$10,000 has not created N$10,000 of profit if wages, food, energy and other costs must still be paid.",
