      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Local linkages can spread part of the spending. A lodge purchasing vegetables from nearby growers supports demand for their produce; a guide purchasing repairs supports a local workshop. Those recipients may make further purchases locally. The strength of these links depends on the availability, quality, quantity and price of local supplies. A destination cannot claim a large local multiplier merely because a tourist made one payment.",
