      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-04",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Leakage occurs when part of tourism spending leaves the area being assessed, for example through imported goods or payments to external suppliers. The boundary matters: a purchase from elsewhere in Namibia leaves a particular village's economy but not necessarily the national economy. Be clear whether the question concerns a settlement, region or country. Leakage reduces retention within that boundary but does not erase all local benefits from the original activity.",
      "claim_ids": [
