    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-05",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A hypothetical spending account shows the distinction. An enterprise receives N$20,000 and makes N$8,000 of payments to local workers and suppliers, N$7,000 outside the area and retains N$5,000 before any other specified obligations. The record establishes those flows, not that every retained dollar reaches households equally. If the account does not state complete costs, ownership or distribution, do not turn the retained amount into a precise profit or poverty-reduction claim.\n\n![Hypothetical spending account: local payments, leakage and retained balance](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-2.3-014-INTERP-answer.png)",
