    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Infrastructure includes access roads, communications, electricity, water supply and waste services. Investment motivated partly by tourism can also help residents if facilities are shared and usable. A road may reduce travel time for both visitors and local producers. A water system may serve an attraction and neighbouring households. The local benefit is conditional on access, capacity, cost and management, rather than established by the mere existence of the installation.",
