    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-10",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Tourist facilities include accommodation, restaurants, visitor centres, toilets, recreation areas and information services. Facilities can support longer stays, safer visits or new enterprises, while some may also be used by residents. A facility's usefulness depends on demand, maintenance and access. An expensive building with little use may create costs instead of the expected benefit. Distinguish a planned service from an operating service and an operating service from demonstrated community access.",
