    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Tourism can strengthen incentives to protect wildlife or landscapes where local people receive worthwhile benefits from maintaining them. Fees, enterprise income or employment can help fund management or make conservation-compatible land uses more attractive. This is a conditional link between value and decisions, not proof that every tourism venture protects nature. Visitor pressure, governance and the distribution of costs still need examination.",
      "claim_ids": [
