    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Community-conservancy tourism in Namibia provides a case for examining these pathways. Ministry information describes contractual payments, employment and training associated with community tourism ventures. Joint ventures can combine community rights and local participation with private operating skills or investment. These are mechanisms of benefit; the existence of an agreement does not establish that payments were timely, benefits were equitable or every household became better off.",
