    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The June 2017 MCC evaluation of Namibia's Conservancy Support Activity illustrates the need to separate levels of outcome. It reported investment and employment gains while noting that broad household income or expenditure increases were not generally established by its analysis. The dated finding does not describe every conservancy today. It shows why increased enterprise activity should not automatically be translated into an identical gain for all households.",
