    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-15",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Benefits can differ among stakeholders. An employed guide may gain wages, a local farmer may gain a customer, a conservancy may receive a contractual payment and a neighbouring household may receive little direct income. Those differences matter when judging development. Ask who receives the flow, when, under what agreement and with what costs. A supported conclusion can recognise real gains while avoiding a claim of uniform benefit.",
      "claim_ids": [
