    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A benefit account should be compared over matching periods and units. Employment counts, monthly receipts, annual bed nights and household income are different measures. A chart showing rising visits and employment can establish a shared trend, but not prove that tourism alone caused every job increase. Supporting business records, supplier evidence or interviews may strengthen the explanation. Keep observed change separate from a proposed causal interpretation.",
