    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The useful overall question is therefore how tourism connects visitor demand to lasting local opportunities. Locally suitable sourcing, training, shared infrastructure and accountable agreements can improve those connections. Their success needs evidence of delivery and outcomes over time. This framework supports a judgement of tourism's contribution without treating revenue, profit, employment and household welfare as interchangeable totals.",
      "claim_ids": [
