    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-18",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Jobs can be compared more accurately when the time dimension is recorded. Suppose one service employs four people throughout the year, while another hires twelve for one month. The second has a larger peak headcount, but that does not establish greater annual employment. Contract length and hours are needed for a comparable work measure. Pay and access to the opportunities matter when the question concerns household welfare rather than staffing levels alone.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.3.05-1",
        "CL-6137-2.3.05-2",
