    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-19",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Infrastructure can serve several purposes. A road used by visitors may also connect residents to schools, health services or markets. Those shared benefits need evidence that the route is accessible and useful for the relevant journeys. A privately restricted facility may offer much less shared benefit than a public connection. Likewise, electricity brought to an enterprise does not prove neighbouring homes can afford or access a connection. The pathway from installation to household benefit should be made explicit.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.3.05-1",
        "CL-6137-2.3.05-2",
