    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-20",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Facilities may produce social value without being a direct cash payment. A maintained public toilet can improve visitor and resident amenity; a local information centre can support navigation and interpretation. Costs still exist, including staffing, water and cleaning. To judge a facility, compare use and service quality with the objective, not simply the construction cost or building size. Maintaining a modest suitable service can be more useful than operating an oversized underused one.",
      "claim_ids": [
