    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-21",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Cultural exchange also has a process. Hosts choose what they wish to share, explain meanings and receive visitors under agreed conditions. Visitors can learn and purchases can support chosen craft work. These benefits depend on respectful participation and a fair arrangement. A performance count or souvenir-sales total alone does not establish mutual understanding, preservation of meaning or consent. If the claim concerns those outcomes, appropriate host perspectives are necessary.",
