    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.3.05-22",
      "block_type": "cross_link",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Tourism statistics should therefore be read as indicators with boundaries. A chart of local supplier payments helps assess one linkage; a wage record helps assess employment income; a visitor survey helps assess experience. Combining relevant records can support a wider conclusion, but each still measures a particular part. A benefit claim becomes stronger through matched evidence, not by repeating the arrival total in several different forms.",
      "claim_ids": [
